---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
<Fragment slot="meta">
  <title>Blog | ScoreBreak</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Updates, announcements, and insights from the ScoreBreak team." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="Blog | ScoreBreak" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Updates, announcements, and insights from the ScoreBreak team." />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://scorebreak.io/blog/index.html" />
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://scorebreak.io/logos/logo-nav.png" />
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="Blog | ScoreBreak" />
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="Updates, announcements, and insights from the ScoreBreak team." />
</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="head">
  <style is:inline>
    /* ── Hero ── */
    .blog-hero {
      padding: calc(var(--nav-h) + 4.5rem) 0 3rem;
      text-align: center;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .blog-hero .section-label { font-size: .9rem; }
    .blog-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: -.04em;
      line-height: 1.12;
      margin: 1rem auto 1.25rem;
      position: relative;
    }
    .blog-hero-sub {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
      max-width: 560px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      position: relative;
    }

    /* ── Post list ── */
    .post-list { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .post-entry { padding: 2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-sub); }
    .post-entry:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-sub); }
    .post-entry-meta {
      font-size: .75rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: .1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin-bottom: .6rem;
    }
    .post-entry h2 {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -.02em;
      line-height: 1.3;
      margin-bottom: .6rem;
    }
    .post-entry h2 a { transition: color .2s; }
    .post-entry h2 a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
    .post-entry-excerpt {
      font-size: .98rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .blog-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 8vw, 2.6rem); }
      .post-entry h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; }
    }
  </style>
</Fragment>

<section class="blog-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Blog</div>
    <h1>Make the Change.</h1>
    <p class="blog-hero-sub">Updates, announcements, and insights from the ScoreBreak team.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     POSTS
══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top:1rem;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="post-list">
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2023-04-02">April 2, 2023</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Jordan Hendry</div>
        <h2><a href="v6-recordable-film-sessions.html">v6 - Recordable Film Sessions</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">Today, we&#x27;re introducing version 6 of ScoreBreak for iOS, iPadOS, and macOS.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2023-04-02">April 2, 2023</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Jordan Hendry</div>
        <h2><a href="scorebreak-version-60-recordable-film-sessions.html">ScoreBreak version 6.0 to enhance coaching solutions with Recordable Film Sessions</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">ScoreBreak, a leading sports technology startup, has announced the release of version 6 of its iOS, iPadOS, and macOS software, featuring an innovative recordable film session feature.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2023-03-29">March 29, 2023</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Jordan Hendry</div>
        <h2><a href="looking-back-at-scorebreak-version-5.html">Looking back at ScoreBreak version 5: A comprehensive update</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">ScoreBreak version 5 was active from December 29, 2021, to March 30, 2023, for a total of 457 days.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2022-11-29">November 29, 2022</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Jordan Hendry</div>
        <h2><a href="notes-all-over.html">Notes all over</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">ScoreBreak version 5.2 focuses on the experience of taking notes on clips.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2022-06-02">June 2, 2022</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Jordan Hendry</div>
        <h2><a href="scorebreak-chat-v2.html">ScoreBreak Chat v2</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">Staying in communication is instrumental to your team&#x27;s development, organization, and performance.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2022-01-24">January 24, 2022</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Tommy Wright</div>
        <h2><a href="scorebreak-web-v4.html">ScoreBreak Web v4</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">ScoreBreak Web App v4 is an update focused on power user tools for content creation and advanced editing interactions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="post-entry">
        <div class="post-entry-meta"><time datetime="2022-01-04">January 4, 2022</time> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Jordan Hendry</div>
        <h2><a href="scorebreak-v5.html">ScoreBreak v5</a></h2>
        <p class="post-entry-excerpt">An ode to professional coaches, Version 5 extends upon ScoreBreak&#x27;s foundation with powerful new features and functionalities.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
